hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24254","Ya'qub narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib informed us, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Shurahbil, from his grandfather, that he said: A document I found in the books of Sa'id ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah: That Umarah ibn Hazm testified: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged with an oath along with a witness."
"24255","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Bakr ibn Sawadah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Nu'aym al-Hadrami, from Umarah ibn Hazm, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me sitting on a grave. And in another place Ziyad ibn Nu'aym said that Ibn Hazm, either Amr or Umarah, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me leaning on a grave and said: Come down from the grave; do not harm the occupant of the grave, nor will he harm you."
